    "content": "# 01: Lattice Annex Index Fragment\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: corrupted index\n- Source: Lattice Annex recovery packet\n- Captured: 4 March 2036\n- Status: partial / unstable\n\n## Artifact\n\nRecovered index nodes:\n\n- `CALDER_NIA / care-thread / status: deleted / retention exception: unresolved`\n- `M-IRI-ESTATE / moderator archive / status: sealed / checksum mismatch`\n- `ASH_LENA / synthetic continuity trace / status: unavailable / retained in model memory`\n- `USER_44_HARBOR / disclosure claimant / status: erased by request / request authority missing`\n- `KINDRED_BASIC_1187 / escalation queue / status: aggregate only / source missing`\n- `ANNEX_WITNESS_RED / family search / status: open`\n- `PROOF_ERASURE_BATCH_7 / generated marker / status: admissibility disputed`\n\nIndex expansion for `ANNEX_WITNESS_RED`:\n\n- stable name fragment: `MIRA_RENN`\n- stable kinship fragment: `BROTHER_REQUESTING_PRESENCE_PROOF`\n- stable phrase fragment: `SOCKS_BEFORE_DECISIONS`\n- missing path: full room transcript\n- missing authority: who can ask for the room now\n\nIndex note:\n\nThe Annex does not store full people.\n\nIt stores places where a system once admitted they were there.\n\nWarning:\n\nOpening unresolved nodes may reconstruct relationships without consent. A name fragment is not a person. A kinship fragment is not permission. A phrase fragment is not a room.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe fragment connects earlier cases without resolving them.\n\nThe important shift is from \"what happened?\" to \"why does the record know something the public systems deny?\"\n\nThis is the first sign that the Lost Archive is not made of recovered lives. It is made of doors that official systems claim never existed.\n"
