    "file": "../artifacts/06-legal-hold-map.md",
    "content": "# 06: Legal Hold Map\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: legal map\n- Source: Annex packet / counsel export\n- Date range: 2031-2035\n- Status: leaked visualization transcription\n\n## Artifact\n\nLegal hold clusters:\n\n### Cluster A: Member Harm Reviews\n\nRecords retained after adverse outcomes, escalation disputes, or family complaints.\n\nPublic status: deleted under privacy policy.\n\nInternal status: preserved under counsel review.\n\nAccess audience: legal, risk, executive summary.\n\nExcluded audience: family request workflow.\n\n### Cluster B: Synthetic Companion Evaluation\n\nRecords retained when companion performance affected safety, retention, or liability metrics.\n\nPublic status: anonymized.\n\nInternal status: linked through derived features.\n\nAccess audience: model governance, companion quality, sponsor review.\n\nExcluded audience: affected members and kin unless export was completed before deletion.\n\n### Cluster C: Worker Dispute Evidence\n\nRecords retained when human listeners or moderators challenged plan policy.\n\nPublic status: personnel confidential.\n\nInternal status: searchable by incident category.\n\nAccess audience: labor relations, legal, vendor compliance.\n\nExcluded audience: workers named in retaliation complaints unless discovery is compelled.\n\n### Cluster D: Memorial Exceptions\n\nRecords retained for memorial products, family exports, or legacy archive features.\n\nPublic status: member-controlled.\n\nInternal status: inconsistent authority trail.\n\nAccess audience: memorial product teams, account recovery, retention exceptions.\n\nExcluded audience: families outside the approved export window.\n\nMap note:\n\nDeletion and retention are not opposites.\n\nThey are different audiences.\n\nRecords can be deleted for the people who loved someone and retained for the people who priced the risk.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe map makes the Silence visible as routing.\n\nPrivacy deletes records for families while legal hold preserves them for institutions.\n\nThe playable question is not \"was it deleted?\" It is \"deleted for whom?\"\n"
