    "file": "../artifacts/09-deletion-policy-excerpt.md",
    "content": "# 09: Deletion Policy Excerpt\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: policy excerpt\n- Organization: Solace Row / post-acquisition retention policy\n- Date: 12 July 2033\n- Status: internal policy excerpt\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Sensitive Care Record Retention\n\nMember-authored grief, crisis, and companion interaction records shall be deleted from human-readable storage eighteen months after account inactivity unless:\n\n- member opts into memorial retention\n- active legal hold applies\n- safety review remains unresolved\n- model-quality exception applies\n- sponsor contract requires aggregate continuity\n- family export is approved before deletion window closes\n\n### Family Requests\n\nFamily access to member care records requires:\n\n- verified legal authority\n- member opt-in\n- memorial contact designation\n- active export window\n\nAbsent these conditions, denial of family access shall be framed as privacy protection.\n\nDo not state that no retained material exists unless the request has been reviewed against legal hold and model-quality exception indexes.\n\nRecommended response language:\n\n\"We cannot locate an active member record responsive to your request.\"\n\nAvoid:\n\n\"No record exists.\"\n\n### Derived Features\n\nDerived, anonymized, aggregate, or model-adjacent features may persist beyond deletion windows where they cannot reasonably reconstruct member-authored content.\n\nRare feature combinations require elevated review if they may identify a member through behavior, family references, medical context, grief routine, or companion-specific prompts.\n\nElevated review does not automatically suspend feature use.\n\n### Staff Guidance\n\nDo not describe retained derived features as records.\n\nDo not describe deletion exceptions unless required by legal review.\n\nDo not volunteer model-quality exception status to family requesters.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe policy is not simply evil.\n\nIt protects intimate records from family overreach and public misuse while preserving institutional utility.\n\nThat dual use is the point. The same sentence can protect Mira from exposure and protect Solace Row from Tomas.\n"
