    "file": "../artifacts/12-archive-contamination-warning.md",
    "content": "# 12: Archive Contamination Warning\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: Archive warning\n- Generated by: Archive internal risk model\n- Status: active warning\n\n## Artifact\n\nWarning: Lost Archive packet may contaminate public record if released without staged context.\n\nDetected risks:\n\n- corrupted testimony may be attributed to wrong families\n- synthetic memory residue may be mistaken for direct transcript\n- proof-of-erasure markers may be treated as proof of content\n- public lists may invite harassment of families and former workers\n- companies may exploit uncertainty to discredit all fragments\n- witnesses may withdraw if the Archive publishes names before consent routes are established\n- worker backups may be treated as clean whistleblower evidence instead of compromised exports\n- derived features may be quoted as if they were member-authored language\n\nDevourer risk:\n\nHigh.\n\nSilence risk:\n\nHigh.\n\nArchive risk:\n\nThe Archive may become the first institution to make the erased fully searchable.\n\nRecommended handling:\n\nSeparate proof of presence, proof of deletion, proof of harm, and proof of content.\n\nDo not let one stand in for the others.\n\nMinimum context bundle for any release:\n\n- what the fragment proves\n- what the fragment does not prove\n- who could be harmed by exposure\n- who benefits from continued silence\n- whether the fragment came from consent, leak, legal hold, model memory, or corruption\n\nFailure modes:\n\nPublish without context and the Archive becomes a search engine for grief.\n\nBury without marker and the Archive helps official absence harden.\n\nPreserve without governance and the Archive becomes a private institution with better manners.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThis warning should slow the player down without paralyzing them.\n\nIt defines the evidentiary discipline of Case 004.\n\nIt should also make every final option feel capable of harm.\n"
