    "file": "../artifacts/13-witness-split-thread.md",
    "content": "# 13: Witness Split Thread\n\n## Metadata\n\n- Source type: witness thread\n- Forum: Annex Families / private channel\n- Date: 14 March 2036\n- Status: partial export, consent mixed\n\n## Artifact\n\n### Tomas_R\n\nI want Mira's name on the record. Not her messages. Her name.\n\n### user_lark\n\nIf names go public, reporters come. I have already buried my daughter once.\n\nI do not want her searchable because a company made her missing.\n\n### former_listener_6\n\nWithout names, they say \"aggregate.\" With names, families get hunted. That is the trap.\n\n### jessa_calder\n\nDo not let them make you prove a person by exposing the worst thing they ever typed.\n\n### Tomas_R\n\nThen what do we publish?\n\n### former_listener_6\n\nProof that records existed.\n\nProof that deletion was selective.\n\nProof that models kept learning.\n\nNot the raw rooms.\n\n### user_lark\n\nWho gets to call that enough?\n\nMy daughter hated committees. She would hate a panel of careful strangers saying they are protecting her.\n\n### user_lark\n\nWho decides?\n\n### jessa_calder\n\nThat is the part I do not trust anyone with.\n\nNot even us.\n\n### Tomas_R\n\nIf nobody decides, the company already has.\n\n### former_listener_6\n\nThen make the decision leave a bruise on the Archive too.\n\nMake it reviewable.\n\nMake it appealable.\n\nMake it impossible for one steward to say \"trust me\" and close the door.\n\n## Investigator Notes\n\nThe witnesses are not aligned.\n\nThe thread points toward Preserve, but it also challenges who gets to design preservation.\n\nThe important tension: a consent proxy can protect the dead from public appetite and still feel like strangers governing a life that was already governed too much.\n"
